#uuid "d0319ad1-03eb-5a51-a67c-e55d25763f00" 13194139534180 true] [17592186280896 1034 "44" 13194139534180 true] [17592186280896 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534180 true] [17592186280896 1111 #uuid "190df470-cb21-5f5f-a0c6-768f6bd8a7f0" 13194139534180 true] [17592186280897 1017 #edb/ref 17592186280898 13194139534180 true] [17592186280897 1089 "q-280519" 13194139534180 true] [17592186280897 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534180 true] [17592186280897 1100 "Given that $G=[\\begin{aligned}x & 2x-1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & x+1 & -4\\end{aligned}]$ is singular, find the value of $x.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534180 true] [17592186280897 1113 #uuid "0fc67642-4c1a-5d0b-9b18-c66e38eea3ba" 13194139534180 true] [17592186280897 1145 "Let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det & =|\\begin{aligned}x & 2x-1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & x+1 & -4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =x|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ x+1 & -4\\end{aligned}|-(2x-1)|\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -4\\end{aligned}|+6|\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ -1 & x+1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =x(3\\cdot (-4)-0\\cdot (x+1))-(2x-1)(0)+6(0\\cdot (x+1)-3\\cdot (-1)) \\\\  & =x(-12)+0+6(3) \\\\  & =-12x+18\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the matrix is singular, the determinant is $0,$ and we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-12x+18 & =0 \\\\ -12x & =-18 \\\\ x & =\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534180 true] [17592186280898 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280899 13194139534180 true] [17592186280898 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280900 13194139534180 true] [17592186280898 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534180 true] [17592186280898 1041 "field-1" 13194139534180 true] [17592186280898 1104 #edb/ref 17592186280900 13194139534180 true] [17592186280898 1110 #uuid "6e1bfaa7-81e3-5dbc-937a-0178c987a77c" 13194139534180 true] [17592186280899 1034 "2" 13194139534180 true] [17592186280899 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534180 true] [17592186280899 1111 #uuid "e9f9fcf0-4f20-5133-908f-a1dbf85066a5" 13194139534180 true] [17592186280900 1034 "\\frac{3}{2}" 13194139534180 true] [17592186280900 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534180 true] [17592186280900 1111 #uuid "2fad3e84-073e-5dca-b865-a32ab83df94c" 13194139534180 true] [17592186280901 1017 #edb/ref 17592186280902 13194139534180 true] [17592186280901 1017 #edb/ref 17592186280904 13194139534180 true] [17592186280901 1089 "q-280541" 13194139534180 true] [17592186280901 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534180 true] [17592186280901 1100 "Given that the determinant of $[\\begin{aligned}x & 2x & 5 \\\\ 3 & x & 4 \\\\ 7 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]$ is $40$, find all the possible values of $x$ **in ascending order**.\n\nIn ascending order, $x=$\n{{field-1}} and $x=$\n{{field-2}}." 13194139534180 true] [17592186280901 1113 #uuid "5f431d5d-b965-53ac-8681-9fb78bb22b04" 13194139534180 true] [17592186280901 1145 "Let’s use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}x & 2x & 5 \\\\ 3 & x & 4 \\\\ 7 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =x|\\begin{aligned}x & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|-2x|\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 \\\\ 7 & 2\\end{aligned}|+5|\\begin{aligned}3 & x \\\\ 7 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =x(2x-4)-2x(3\\cdot 2-4\\cdot 7)+5(3-7x) \\\\  & =x(2x-4)-2x(-22)+15-35x \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}-4x+44x+15-35x \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}+5x+15\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the determinant of the matrix is $40$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}+5x+15 & =40 \\\\ 2{x}^{2}+5x-25 & =0 \\\\ x & =\\frac{-5\\pm \\sqrt{{5}^{2}-4(2)(-25)}}{2(2)} \\\\ x & =\\frac{-5+\\sqrt{225}}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{-5\\pm 15}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, **in ascending order**, the solutions are $x=-5$ and $x=\\frac{5}{2}.$" 13194139534180 true] [17592186280902 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280903 13194139534180 true] [17592186280902 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534180 true] [17592186280902 1041 "field-1" 13194139534180 true] [17592186280902 1104 #edb/ref 17592186280903 13194139534180 true] [17592186280902 1110 #uuid "96a1507d-0f5f-57d6-932f-9cdcdc22b501" 13194139534180 true] [17592186280903 1034 "-5" 13194139534180 true] [17592186280903 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534180 true] [17592186280903 1111 #uuid "698fa493-2d03-50fd-bb8f-c1c8495b2b59" 13194139534180 true] [17592186280904 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280905 13194139534180 true] [17592186280904 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534180 true] [17592186280904 1041 "field-2" 13194139534180 true] [17592186280904 1104 #edb/ref 17592186280905 13194139534180 true] [17592186280904 1110 #uuid "bf5590f5-597e-5e73-a790-25380b0453cd" 13194139534180 true] [17592186280905 1034 "\\frac{5}{2}" 13194139534180 true] [17592186280905 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534180 true] [17592186280905 1111 #uuid "6773640e-8024-5910-b766-bb433bbcf121" 13194139534180 true] [17592186280906 1017 #edb/ref 17592186280907 13194139534180 true] [17592186280906 1089 "q-38182" 13194139534180 true] [17592186280906 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534180 true] [17592186280906 1100 "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $Q$ given below?\n\n- $Q$ is **not** a singular matrix\n- $Q$ is a singular matrix\n- $det(Q)=-5$\n\n$$\nQ=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 7 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 8\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139534180 true] [17592186280906 1113 #uuid "4646eada-04b7-5167-b329-286673c2150b" 13194139534180 true] [17592186280906 1145 "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(Q) & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 7 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 8\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0|\\begin{aligned}4 & 7 \\\\ 5 & 8\\end{aligned}|-3|\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 \\\\ 2 & 8\\end{aligned}|+6|\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0-3(8-14)+6(5-8) \\\\  & =0-3\\cdot (-6)+6\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =18-18 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(Q)=0$, the matrix is singular. \n\nTherefore, only statement II is true." 13194139534180 true] [17592186280907 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280908 13194139534180 true] [17592186280907 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280909 13194139534180 true] [17592186280907 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280910 13194139534180 true] [17592186280907 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280911 13194139534180 true] [17592186280907 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280912 13194139534180 true] [17592186280907 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534180 true] [17592186280907 1041 "selection" 13194139534180 true] [17592186280907 1104 #edb/ref 17592186280912 13194139534180 true] [17592186280907 1110 #uuid "84ed8533-f1fb-5df4-95a9-e6288fd5e96f" 13194139534180 true] [17592186280908 1034 "II and III only" 13194139534180 true] [17592186280908 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534180 true] [17592186280908 1111 #uuid "bb4ba432-2a8f-5769-8c7b-3bf2be07a4ff" 13194139534180 true] [17592186280909 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534180 true] [17592186280909 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534180 true] [17592186280909 1111 #uuid "40bf93a9-0e1a-5d27-a8f0-f3f34430aa2c" 13194139534180 true] [17592186280910 1034 "I only" 13194139534180 true] [17592186280910 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534180 true] [17592186280910 1111 #uuid "1453c279-fab3-529d-aaba-4443449a3b23" 13194139534180 true] [17592186280911 1034 "III only" 13194139534180 true] [17592186280911 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534180 true] [17592186280911 1111 #uuid "a0810cfc-2716-503e-8eda-9bd7b08acab6" 13194139534180 true] [17592186280912 1034 "II only" 13194139534180 true] [17592186280912 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534180 true] [17592186280912 1111 #uuid "ce492c35-85b8-5d30-8cc7-1882be5a74c4" 13194139534180 true] [17592186280913 1017 #edb/ref 17592186280914 13194139534180 true] [17592186280913 1089 "q-69835" 13194139534180 true] [17592186280913 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534180 true] [17592186280913 1100 "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $T$ given below?\n\n- $T$ is a singular matrix\n- $det(T)=-3$\n- $T$ is **not** a singular matrix\n\n \n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139534180 true] [17592186280913 1113 #uuid "0582f249-3bf5-5079-8fe1-8ed6df521a52" 13194139534180 true] [17592186280913 1145 "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(T) & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}|-2|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|-1|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4(2+3)-2(1+6)-1(-1+4) \\\\  & =4\\cdot 5-2\\cdot 7-1\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =20-14-3 \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $det(T)=3\\ne 0$, the matrix is **not** singular. \n\nTherefore, only statement III is true." 13194139534180 true] [17592186280914 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280915 13194139534180 true] [17592186280914 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280916 13194139534180 true] [17592186280914 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280917 13194139534180 true] [17592186280914 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280918 13194139534180 true] [17592186280914 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280919 13194139534180 true] [17592186280914 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534180 true] [17592186280914 1041 "selection" 13194139534180 true] [17592186280914 1104 #edb/ref 17592186280917 13194139534180 true] [17592186280914 1110 #uuid "6b828eb5-1cb6-5083-bcd2-dee4ad1a5979" 13194139534180 true] [17592186280915 1034 "II and III only" 13194139534180 true] [17592186280915 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534180 true] [17592186280915 1111 #uuid "07377c51-5e4f-5116-9e6c-1c1e54ce83f1" 13194139534180 true] [17592186280916 1034 "I only" 13194139534180 true] [1759218628091